   Environmental Management - Tourism, Society and Education Session (Part
   III), Tianjin, PEOPLES R CHINA, NOV 23-24, 2018},
Organization = {TU Bergakademie; Tianjin Univ Finance \& Econ, Pearl River Coll; German
   Acad Exchange Serv Fdn; IMRE Alumni Network},
Abstract = {With the development of China's economy in recent years, the hospitality
   and tourism industries are in a fast development period. Employees are
   significant, because employees deliver service directly to customers
   through face-to-face processes. To better serve customer and improve
   their satisfaction, it is necessary to know how to attract and maintain
   qualified employees working in the industry. The importance of talents
   in the competitions is recognized by the hospitality industry. The
   objective of this paper is to examine which factors have influences on
   career choices within the hospitality and tourism industries in China,
   and to explore the influence of contextual and background information on
   career choices. Independent t-test and regression analysis were
   designated for measuring related variables. Results of the present study
   could assist hospitality students to explore career related information
   and maintain talents in the hospitality industry in China.},
