Abstract = {This study aims to investigate the characteristics and attitudes of
   people who cycle to work in a Brazilian medium-sized city, especially
   focusing on safe cycling context. In loco observation was also conducted
   in order to verify the attitudes and behaviors of cyclists,
   motorcyclists and drivers regarding the Brazilian Traffic Code. The
   results indicate that cycling is a very important transport mode for
   people going to work, but the municipality has a precarious control of
   traffic, there is a lack of relevant legislation to the use of bicycles
   and the Brazilian Traffic Code is frequently violated by motorized and
