Abstract = {Teachers' perception, knowledge and behaviour in inclusive practice
   represent a very important topic of today's world. All the communities
   try to develop inclusive educational systems in order to create an
   inclusive society. But, in spite of this, there are major differences
   between what teachers believe to know about inclusive education, what
   they really know and how they behave in the classroom. At international
   level (Avramidis, Campbell and Gilmore) we can discus about teachers'
   attitudes towards inclusive education, but also about good practice
   examples. At national level, there are also good practice examples such
   as those of Vrasmas and Ghergut. (C) 2013 The Authors. Published by
