   Management Grp; Amer Scholar Press; Jinan Univ, Alumni Assoc},
Abstract = {Today, the convention and exhibition (C\&E) industry is one of the
   fastest growing sectors within service industries, both in a global and
   country specific context, and extensive studies have been conducted in
   this field. With increasingly fierce competition, the topics of
   destinations and/or venues selection and decision-making process have
   received substantial interest, but most of them focused on the
   convention segment and were from the perspective of meeting planners. In
   such a context, this study explored the importance of destination
   attributes to exhibition attendees by conducting a questionnaire survey
   and comparing it with previous studies results. It revealed that there
   were some similarities and differences between the two groups' views
   towards C\&E destinations. The authors also evaluated how Guangzhou (one
   of the three largest convention \& exhibition cities in China) performed
   in respect of those attributes and identified its strengths and
   weaknesses by applying the importance-performance analysis. It is
   suggested that C\&E destinations should put more emphasis on exhibition
   attendees' needs in their promotion program and make adjustment to their
   promotion emphases for different segments.},
