   11-12, 2017},
Abstract = {Traditionally, the research literature regarding family business
   suggests that these businesses hold certain characteristics that offers
   them uniquness and advantages when it comes to customer and stakeholders
   relationships (Blomback, 2011; Carrigan and Buckley, 2008a; Cooper et
   al., 2005; Okoroafo and Koh, 2009). The general perceptions of consumers
   represent the general framework in which businesses create and promote
   their brand and this framework influences the decisions regarding the
   selection of elements to be included in the brand (Blomback, 2011). The
   sociocultural context influences the way family is perceived and as a
   consequence the way family business is viewed. In this context, this
   paper aims to explore the perceptions of Romanian consumers regarding
   the phrase ``family firm{''} using constructs and scales that have been
   developed and validated in the research literature (Binz et al. 2013;
   Fombrun et al. 2000). The objective of this study is to assess whether
   there is a distinct image regarding family business in the national
   context of Romania's consumer market and to identify the specific
   associations consumers hold in this geo-cultural areal.},
