Abstract = {Within a project aimed at evaluating the landslide risk in several
   villages of Southern Italy, the case of Plataci, located in
   north-eastern Calabria, is here examined. After a brief description of
   geology and geomorphology of the study area, with particular reference
   to the state of activity of the slope movements, a zonation of landslide
   damage to buildings in the urban area (carried out according to a
   recently proposed classification scheme) is presented. Comparing the
   results from the geomorphological survey and the landslide damage
   zonation helped to discuss slope movement vulnerability at Plataci.},
