Note = {2nd Advanced Research on Business, Management and Humanities (ARBUHUM),
   Phuket, THAILAND, OCT 10-12, 2017},
Organization = {Malaysia Tech Scientist Assoc},
Abstract = {This paper aims to explore novice teachers' perceptions on Teaching and
   Learning (TnL) support they receive when they start their teaching
   career. The research was carried out on 30 novice teachers teaching at
   primary and secondary schools in Perlis. Data were collected using
   face-to-face interview with the research participants. The findings
   showed that novice teachers received support from experience teachers,
   mentors, colleague, excellent teachers and teachers from other parties.
   They received support in the forms of advice on teaching techniques,
   tips on classroom control, sharing of teaching aids, explanation on
   subject content, and guidance on the correct way to write Daily Lesson
   Plans. Findings also indicated that novice teachers also received
   support from School Improvement Specialist Coaches (SiSC+) and teachers
   form other schools. From the novice teachers' perceptions, they need
   support from various parties to improve their TnL quality in guiding
   using latest method in teaching and learning methods. Novice teachers'
   professional development programmes at the school level should be
   carried out more with the involvement of the relevant parties to ensure
   these novice teachers receive the necessary guidance for a quality TnL.},
