Note = {Conference on Advanced Research on Business, Management and Humanities
   (ARBUHUM), Bandung, INDONESIA, MAR 15-17, 2016},
Organization = {Malaysia Tech Scientist Assoc},
Abstract = {Malaysia has a (64\%) majority Muslim population. It is imperative that
   Islamic schools be provided because vernacular schools have limited
   curriculum capacity to accommodate the Islamic teachings on daily basis.
   Hence, examining the provision of Islamic schools, their physical
   conditions and educational facilities, including laboratories and
   libraries is essential to establish the existence and severity of issues
   and problems facing these schools as well as to ensure their relevance
   and sustainability. Data was collected primarily through questionnaire
   surveys on parents' and teachers' perception of the students'
   performance and also secondarily from analysis of contents of published
   documents and site inventories. Inadequacy of such inventoried
   facilities was one of the major findings. Apparently, some levels of
   financial and monetary assistance were indeed necessary to improve the
   physical conditions of schools, as well as guaranteeing the schools
   longevity. In essence, the findings conform to literature regarding the
   propagation of students' educational performance being indeed influenced
   by the state of both physical and infrastructure provision. It is hence,
   suggested that financial aids targeting on the renovation and upgrading
   of these provision be promptly initiated.},
