   01-03, 2015},
Organization = {Joannes Kepler Univ; Univ Appl Sci; Gmunden Keramik Stadt; Traunsee
   Salzkammergut},
Abstract = {Emotions are omnipresent in our lives. They influence our health,
   decision making, and social interactions-bilateral as well as
   multilateral. Hence also modern forms of opinion building and exchange,
   e.g., on e-participation platforms, should consider the effects of
   emotions on individual and group level. Previous research on group
   interactions demonstrated that providing the members with information
   about the affective state of the entire group, reciprocally influences
   the affective states of the individuals and can even increase group
   performance. Hence, in the current short paper we propose group affect
   live biofeedback (LBF) as a beneficial feature for e-participation
   platforms. We want to examine how group affect LBF based on the
   participant's heart rate impacts participation behavior.},
