   Skiathos Isl, GREECE, OCT 01-03, 2003},
Organization = {Wessex Inst Technol; Univ Thessaly, Dept Planning \& Reg Dev, Sch Engn;
   Municipal Skiathos; Univ Thessaly, Res Comm; TEE Magnisia Reg Sect;
   Sovel; Themeliodomi SA; Coca Cola HBC},
Abstract = {In the framework of this paper a case study is presented concerning a
   combined land-use transport plan in a traffic-congested urban area. The
   area under examination is found in the N.E. part of the municipality of
   Thessaloniki. In the existing situation it includes a variety of land
   uses and is surrounded by heavily dense residential areas. The
   authorities decided to redesign the existing land-use system so as to
   minimize traffic and associate environmental impacts and, at the same
   time, to improve the quality of the environment and the quality of life
   for residents, employees and visitors. The proposed land-use changes
   led, as expected, to the need for the redesign of the transportation
   system so as to adequately serve trips in the ``after{''} situation.
   More especially there was a need for measures to reduce all costs of
   traffic movements including the environmental costs. The general idea
   behind the measures proposed to support the new land-use system is to
   promote sustainable mobility.},
