   ANGELES, CA, AUG 11-16, 1994},
Organization = {Amer Psychol Assoc},
Abstract = {There is great variation regarding the concepts of religiosity and
   spirituality in the psychology of religion literature. In an attempt to
   clarify these constructs in the general population, 16 college students
   were recruited for a task of concept mapping to elicit their perceptions
   of what the designations spiritual person and religious person mean.
   Many positive character traits were used to describe both religious and
   spiritual people. However, participants described spiritual people with
   an emphasis on intellectual activities and inner peace, placing less
   emphasis on external, physical characteristics than their descriptions
   of religious people. Broader dimensions underlying participants'
   descriptions are also discussed.},
