   Environm Technol SA},
Abstract = {It is widely recognised that there is a strong relationship between
   transport and land use planning. The distribution of various land uses
   in both the urban and suburban areas generates transport, and affects
   the travel patterns. One aspect of planning involves architectural
   projects and proposals that seek to create and enhance social or green
   space in urban areas. Social space in Greece is often related to the
   traditional squares, which demand pedestrianisation of the roads around
   them. In this paper we try to evaluate the environmental impacts of the
   pedestrianisation of Kleanthous street, as part of an architectural
   proposal for the restoration of Alana Toumbas Square in Thessaloniki,
   with the use of a traffic simulation model, called SATURN.},
