   AUG 20-25, 1994},
Organization = {Amer Fisheries Soc},
Abstract = {This study analyses an oceanic fishery in southern New England as a
   subculture whose features are adaptive to the total environment in which
   it operates. It is possible to explain how fishers' perceptions of
   safety regulations stem largely from pervasive cultural themes. It is
   suggested that voluntary compliance with safety regulations can be
   enhanced if policy makers utilize knowledge of the subculture and
   involve fishers in the policy-making process.},
