Organization = {INT ASSOC LANDSCAPE ECOL},
Abstract = {The delta system depends on an interaction of physical and human factors
   throughout the whole river basin. The delta is also characterized by the
   quantity of sediment, the course of its branches, the pre-delta, the
   coast and the delta plain. The latter is a wetland with high biological
   productivity and high ecological value. Each of these environments
   presents its characteristic landscape. During its history, the Po delta
   system has experienced frequent flooding, which has resulted in the flow
   being artificially restricted to a few canals with consequent landscape
   changes. The canalization was often associated with land reclamation.
   which accentuated the problem of subsidence. The management of the delta
   depends on national and regional landscape-environmental legislation, a
   regional landscape plan and infraregional schemes. The Po Delta Regional
   Park, in Emilia-Romagna, is composed of six areas of special
   landscape-environmental interest called `stazioni'. A variety of
   natural, historical and cultural elements, involving animals, pine
   woods, valleys, castles, parish churches, homesteads and historical
   centres, can be found in the Po delta landscape. Unfortunately, of the
   different projects proposed in the last 20 years for the establishment
   of the park, none has been realized. Management will become active after
   the approval of the Territorial Plan for the Po Delta Park, now under
   study by the Ferrara Provincial Administration. One of the main
   objectives of this plan is to conserve the memory of past conditions of
   life and activities. The Technical Scientific Committee and the
   Management Union of the Po Delta Regional Park are the bodies
   responsible for developing and protecting the park.},
