   Int Journal Sustainable Dev \& Planning; Wessex Inst Technol},
Abstract = {The main purpose of this paper is to highlight the role of the Strategic
   Environmental Assessment (SEA) process applied to urban and territorial
   planning, as a paradigm of sustainable planning, in order to reconcile
   environmental protection with the development of cities and the
   territory.
   The SEA is analyzed as an instrument for achieving sustainable
   development and, with this purpose, those existing elements in the
   territory that affect territorial and urban planning must be detected
   and must be considered in the SEA process. This includes factors,
   conditions and environmental risks that have to be detected in the
   initial phase of SEA (identification).
   The right to enjoy an appropriate environment and the duty to preserve
   it requires the authorities to ensure the rational use of all natural
   resources, in order to articulate through land-use and urban planning,
   more sustainable cities and territories, being essential for achieving
   this purpose, a proper assessment of the plan.},
